        "faq_tb4y9R": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Are your books political? Do they teach the conservative republican view?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Our books lean towards our Libertarian roots. These books do have a conservative perspective on personal freedom, free markets, property rights, limited government, etc.</p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_KRNdRF": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Are your books religious?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Each of our children’s books is based on an original book or essay—we take classic content and turn it into something accessible for a child.<br/><br/>The first book we did is based on The Law, an essay written in 1850 by a French economist named Frédéric Bastiat.In this essay, Bastiat argues that God is the source of our rights. (A popular opinion at the time, of course.) As such, our book explains the same thing, since we stick with what the original author talked about.<br/><br/>Not all families agree with this, of course—so the secular families reading our books simply take the opportunity to explain that while this is a popular perspective, it’s not one that they share. And that’s fine!<br/><br/>But this is the only book in the children’s series that contains any religious reference; the remaining books—<a href=\"/pages/products\" title=\"Tuttle Twins Books and Products\">see the list here</a>—have no religious content of any kind.<br/><br/>Here is a link to see how Connor answers this question: <br/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/WllQVKPo-e4\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://youtu.be/WllQVKPo-e4\">https://youtu.be/WllQVKPo-e4</a></p>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        },
        "faq_BFVHei": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>What reading level are your books?</p>",
            "text_size": "medium",
            "text_weight": "bold",
            "answer": "<p>Here are some of our samples and age levels: <br/></p><ul><li>Free Market Curriculum (Kindergarten-High school): <a href=\"/pages/economics\" title=\"Life-Changing Education for Children of All Ages\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/economics</a></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Our history book (ages 12 and up): <a href=\"/pages/history\" title=\"History\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/history</a></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Tuttle Twins magazine issue 0 (ages 5-12):  <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0655/8951/0282/files/Issue-0-Digital.pdf?v=1740208911\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0655/8951/0282/files/Issue-0-Digital.pdf?v=1740208911\">https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0655/8951/0282/files/Issue-0-Digital.pdf</a></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Our teen Guidebooks (ages 12 and up) : <a href=\"/pages/guide\" title=\"Tuttle Twins Guidebooks\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/guide</a></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Graphic Novels (ages 8 and up) : <a href=\"/collections/cartoon\" title=\"Cartoon\">https://tuttletwins.com/collections/cartoon</a><br/></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Children’s book Series (ages 5-11): <a href=\"/pages/childrens-resources\" title=\"Children's Resources (Age 5–11)\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/childrens-resources</a><br/></li></ul><p></p><ul><li>Toddler books (ages 0-4): <a href=\"/collections/tuttle-toddlers\" title=\"Tuttle Toddlers\">https://tuttletwins.com/collections/tuttle-toddlers</a></li></ul><p><a href=\"/collections/tuttle-toddlers\" title=\"Tuttle Toddlers\"><br/></a></p><p>Can I view a sample of your children’s books before purchasing?</p><ul><li>Children’s book Series (ages 5-11): <a href=\"/pages/childrens-resources\" title=\"Children's Resources (Age 5–11)\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/childrens-resources</a></li></ul><p></p><p><br/>Can I view a sample of your history book before purchasing?</p><ul><li>Here is the link for a sample of our history: <a href=\"/pages/history\" title=\"History\">https://tuttletwins.com/pages/history</a><br/><br/>If you scroll down on the page you will be able to download a chapter of the History book to look over.</li></ul>",
            "text_size_b": "medium",
            "text_weight_b": "regular"
          }
        }
      },
